---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { SITE } from "../site.config.js";
import { breadcrumbSchema } from "../lib/schema.js";

const crumbs = [{ name: "Privacy Policy", path: "/privacy/" }];
const schema = [breadcrumbSchema(crumbs)];
---

<Base
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description={`How ${SITE.name} handles your data: no calculator inputs are collected, ads load only after you accept cookies, and how to use your privacy rights.`}
  schema={schema}
  crumbs={crumbs}
>
  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-12 lg:py-16">
    <div class="bg-white rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 p-8 sm:p-12 shadow-sm prose prose-slate max-w-none text-sm text-slate-700 leading-relaxed">
      <h1 class="text-3xl font-extrabold text-slate-900 not-prose">Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="text-xs text-slate-500">Effective Date: January 1, 2026 | Last Updated: November 2026</p>

      <hr class="my-6" />

      <h2>1. What we do not collect</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>We do not collect, store, or transmit your financial inputs.</strong> Every calculation on {SITE.name}, including hourly rates, annual salaries, tax filing statuses, and overtime hours, runs inside your own web browser with client-side JavaScript. The numbers you type are not sent to our servers. We have no user accounts and no sign-up form, and we do not ask for your name or address to use the calculators or read the articles.
      </p>

      <h2>2. Information collected automatically</h2>
      <p>
        Like most websites, our hosting provider (Cloudflare Pages) records standard server logs such as IP addresses, browser types, referring pages, and access times. We use them only for security, abuse prevention, and keeping the site running. We do not use third-party analytics or advertising trackers of our own.
      </p>

      <h2 id="cookies">3. Advertising and cookies</h2>
      <p>
        This site is intended to show ads served by Google AdSense and its advertising partners. <strong>The ad code is not loaded until you click Accept on the cookie message.</strong> If you click Reject, or make no choice, no ad script is requested and no advertising cookies are set by this site. Your choice is saved in your browser (local storage) so you are not asked again.
        <button type="button" id="reopen-consent" class="underline text-brand-700 cursor-pointer">Change your choice</button> (reload the page to apply a withdrawal of consent).
      </p>
      <p>If you accept, ads are shown, and:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Third-party vendors, including Google, use cookies to serve ads based on your prior visits to this website or other websites.</li>
        <li>Google uses the DoubleClick advertising cookie (also called the DART cookie) on sites that use AdSense. It lets Google and its partners serve ads based on your visits to this site and others, and it is also used to measure ads and prevent fraud.</li>
        <li>You can opt out of personalized advertising at Google's <a href="https://adssettings.google.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Ads Settings</a>. You can also opt out of some third-party vendors' use of cookies for personalized advertising at <a href="https://www.aboutads.info/choices/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">aboutads.info</a>.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        For more on how Google uses data from sites that use its services, see <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">How Google uses information from sites or apps that use our services</a>. Visitors everywhere, including the European Economic Area, the United Kingdom and Switzerland, are asked for consent before any advertising cookies are used.
      </p>

      <h2>4. Your privacy rights</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>EU, EEA, UK and Switzerland (GDPR):</strong> the legal basis for advertising cookies is your consent, which you can withdraw at any time. You may have the right to access, correct, delete, restrict, or object to the processing of your personal data, to receive a copy of it, and to complain to your data protection authority.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>California and other US states (CCPA/CPRA and similar laws):</strong> you may have the right to know what personal information is collected about you, to request its deletion or correction, and to opt out of the sale or sharing of personal information for targeted advertising. Choosing Reject on the cookie message keeps advertising cookies off.
      </p>
      <p>
        To make a request, email <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>. Because we do not keep accounts or your calculator inputs, there is usually little personal data to give you, and we will tell you so within 30 days.
      </p>

      <h2>5. Children</h2>
      <p>
        This site is written for adults who work, hire, or budget. It is not directed at children under 13, and we do not knowingly collect personal information from them.
      </p>

      <h2>6. Links to other sites</h2>
      <p>
        Articles link to government agencies and other organizations as sources. Their privacy practices are their own.
      </p>

      <h2>7. Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>
        When this policy changes, we update the date at the top of the page.
      </p>

      <h2>8. Contact</h2>
      <p>
        For questions about this policy, email <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <script is:inline>
    (function () {
      var b = document.getElementById("reopen-consent");
      if (!b) return;
      b.addEventListener("click", function () {
        try { localStorage.removeItem("thewagereport_consent_accepted"); } catch (e) {}
        window.dispatchEvent(new CustomEvent("thewagereport:reopen-consent"));
      });
    })();
  </script>
</Base>
